ot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{z}}]}_{8}^{a} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{a}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{8}}) \\\\  & =-6(0-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ef2ab87-f78b-5cbd-9be4-0c1ac3448d89" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Improper Integrals With an Unbounded Upper Limit"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64e8a97c-bd31-58a6-ba54-a89ed0b36bd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64e8a97c-bd31-58a6-ba54-a89ed0b36bd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317910} :answer-field/id #uuid "007c463a-09f1-5ff6-9f77-f83fc2551af7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "db36f5e5-41a9-5b43-95cc-4b380f69dbb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-350322" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{18}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{18}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{3}^{a}\\frac{18}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =18{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{3}^{a}{x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =18{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[(-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{-3})]}_{3}^{a} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}]}_{3}^{a} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{{a}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{3}^{3}}) \\\\  & =-6(0-\\frac{1}{27}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319371 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ef2ab87-f78b-5cbd-9be4-0c1ac3448d89" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Improper Integrals With an Unbounded Upper Limit"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c05ccd85-237f-566b-a79f-e8d9590a5726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c05ccd85-237f-566b-a79f-e8d9590a5726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318202} :answer-field/id #uuid "624feba0-3d98-5dfb-b8fe-2f49ece6f4cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318634}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e009094e-338f-5586-9e0b-28bba5f98113" :question/math-academy-id "q-350331" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{8}}}\\,\\text{d}y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{8}}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{8}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =5{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{y}^{-8/3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =5{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{3}{5}{y}^{-5/3}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{5}}}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{a}^{5}}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{1}^{5}}}) \\\\  & =-3(0-1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319372 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ef2ab87-f78b-5cbd-9be4-0c1ac3448d89" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Improper Integrals With an Unbounded Upper Limit"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf7372ff-a95c-5140-9146-b9e95e23882d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf7372ff-a95c-5140-9146-b9e95e23882d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318253} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a052466-0020-5268-9c1b-c0202f71b6a1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318763}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "039703b5-2c46-51fb-a40a-a73595491778" :question/math-academy-id "q-350333" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12}{\\sqrt[3]{{s}^{7}}}\\,\\text{d}s=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12}{\\sqrt[3]{{s}^{7}}}\\,\\text{d}s & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}\\frac{12}{\\sqrt[3]{{s}^{7}}}\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =12{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{s}^{-7/3}\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =12{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{3}{4}{s}^{-4/3}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-9\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{s}^{4}}}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-9\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{a}^{4}}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{1}^{4}}}) \\\\  & =-9(0-1) \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ef2ab87-f78b-5cbd-9be4-0c1ac3448d89" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Improper Integrals With an Unbounded Upper Limit"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4405f0b5-3014-5db5-b9e0-baacfc0fc223" :ans